title: Opposition Strategy
subtitle: How do we resist from the minority?
tags: govt_action
new-page: true
view-if: white_house == "R" and maga >= 20
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 2 capital.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; capital -= 2

= Opposition Strategy

When the other side holds power, the opposition has to decide how to oppose.

- @courts: Litigate. Use the courts and state attorneys general.
- @protest: Support mass mobilization and peaceful protest.
- @cooperate: Cooperate on the issues where we can.
- @states: Build power in the states.

@courts
subtitle: Slow and uneven.
on-arrival: stability += 4; media_trust += 1; enthusiasm += 1

The courts are a brake. Not a steering wheel.

@protest
subtitle: Mass energy, but watch the margins.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 6; far_left += 1; pop_mod += 0.2; stability += 1

The streets fill. Most protesters are peaceful. Some are not.

@cooperate
subtitle: Shows we can govern. Frustrates the base.
on-arrival: mod_dissent -= 4; prog_dissent += 4; enthusiasm -= 2; pop_mod += 0.2; maga -= 1

Governing means finding the votes that exist.

@states
subtitle: Long-term and robust.
on-arrival: stability += 3; pop_mod += 0.2; enthusiasm += 2; house_d += 1

Statehouses become laboratories, and bulwarks.
